WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.093 --> 00:00:13.918
I not believe it.

2
00:00:14.798 --> 00:00:17.339
Tufty had flown out through my skylight!

3
00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:21.221
"Tufty won't be able to find his way home!"

4
00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.481
Molly cried.

5
00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:27.884
"He doesn't have a bell like I do," said Caswell sadly.

6
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.724
"Even if someone finds him, they won't know he's my parrot," Molly went on.

7
00:00:35.645 --> 00:00:37.306
Her eyes filled with tears.

8
00:00:37.326 --> 00:00:40.969
"I'll never see Tufty again!"

9
00:00:44.032 --> 00:00:47.094
We ran into the living room and told my mom what had happened.

10
00:00:48.155 --> 00:00:49.176
My mom sat down.

11
00:00:49.777 --> 00:00:50.557
She looked worried.

12
00:00:50.577 --> 00:00:54.460
"Are you sure Tufty flew through the skylight?"

13
00:00:54.861 --> 00:00:55.461
she asked.

14
00:00:55.481 --> 00:01:00.189
"We looked all over my room," I said, "and he's not there."

15
00:01:00.209 --> 00:01:02.711
"Go find Mr.

16
00:01:02.751 --> 00:01:04.953
Calabria," my mom said.

17
00:01:04.973 --> 00:01:07.775
"See if he'll help us look for Tufty."

18
00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:10.517
We found Mr.

19
00:01:10.558 --> 00:01:12.179
Calabria in his workshop.

20
00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.681
He smiled when he saw us.

21
00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.803
"Good news, everybody.

22
00:01:17.223 --> 00:01:20.345
You'll be able to turn on your air conditioners again tonight!"

23
00:01:20.365 --> 00:01:24.929
"We came to see you about something else," Molly explained.

24
00:01:24.949 --> 00:01:28.192
"We need help finding my parrot."

25
00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:32.135
"He flew through my skylight," I explained.

26
00:01:33.716 --> 00:01:35.778
"Oh dear," said Mr.

27
00:01:35.838 --> 00:01:38.840
Calabria. "Let's go see if we can spot him."

28
00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:42.443
Everyone except Molly went up to the roof.

29
00:01:43.424 --> 00:01:46.607
Her mom didn't want her to climb the narrow stairs with her boot.

30
00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:52.732
From the roof of our building, you can see all over the city.

31
00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:57.476
I could see the tops of apartment buildings and a big bridge.

32
00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:00.710
But I didn't see any sign of Tufty.

33
00:02:02.211 --> 00:02:04.393
We all looked and listened for him.

34
00:02:06.935 --> 00:02:14.281
We heard car horns and subway trains, but this time they were real horns and real trains.

35
00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.924
Mr. Calabria peered down at the street.

36
00:02:19.965 --> 00:02:22.327
"A police car is stopping in front of our building!"

37
00:02:22.828 --> 00:02:23.348
he said.

38
00:02:23.368 --> 00:02:28.112
"I'd better go down and see what the police officers want."

39
00:02:29.088 --> 00:02:30.029
We followed Mr.

40
00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:31.409
Calabria downstairs.

41
00:02:34.891 --> 00:02:37.893
And you'll never believe what happened next!

42
00:02:39.314 --> 00:02:41.355
A policewoman stepped out of the car.

43
00:02:41.815 --> 00:02:43.496
She was holding a big box.

44
00:02:44.737 --> 00:02:46.138
"Do the O'Donnells live here?"

45
00:02:46.618 --> 00:02:47.198
she asked.

46
00:02:47.218 --> 00:02:49.700
"Yes," said Mr.

47
00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.701
Calabria. "Is something wrong?"

48
00:02:52.922 --> 00:02:54.383
The policewoman smiled.

49
00:02:54.403 --> 00:02:56.504
"I have something for them."

50
00:03:00.204 --> 00:03:02.426
I heard a sound from inside the box.

51
00:03:03.867 --> 00:03:05.628
"My number is 555...

52
00:03:05.788 --> 00:03:06.949
I never get it wrong!"

53
00:03:06.969 --> 00:03:10.071
"That's Tufty!"

54
00:03:10.512 --> 00:03:10.992
I cried.

55
00:03:11.012 --> 00:03:13.834
"He's singing Molly's telephone number!"

56
00:03:13.854 --> 00:03:16.096
"He's my parrot!"

57
00:03:16.456 --> 00:03:17.617
said Molly happily.

58
00:03:17.637 --> 00:03:23.341
"We found Tufty in the park," the policewoman explained.

59
00:03:23.361 --> 00:03:27.324
"We were able to trace the telephone number back to Molly's family."

60
00:03:28.332 --> 00:03:30.333
Molly was thrilled to see Tufty.

61
00:03:31.533 --> 00:03:35.055
After that the parrot spent all his time sitting on Molly's walking boot.

62
00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.096
He loved to peck at it.

63
00:03:38.296 --> 00:03:40.717
The rest of the summer went by really fast.

64
00:03:41.798 --> 00:03:43.959
We kept trying to teach Tufty to talk.

65
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.141
But he just kept singing the telephone number song.

66
00:03:50.281 --> 00:03:53.783
Luckily, he never made any more loud noises.

67
00:03:55.063 --> 00:03:56.004
Oh, and guess what.

68
00:03:56.956 --> 00:04:01.638
As soon as our air conditioners started working again, the heat wave was over!

69
00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:05.560
"It's going to get cold tonight," my mom said.

70
00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.781
"We might even need to put on our sweaters."

71
00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:11.982
"Cool!" said Tate.

72
00:04:13.103 --> 00:04:14.864
That made everyone laugh.

73
00:04:19.045 --> 00:04:20.106
Molly grinned at me.

74
00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.387
"I'm glad the heat wave is over.

75
00:04:23.027 --> 00:04:25.048
But I'm also glad we had a heat wave.

76
00:04:25.692 --> 00:04:30.933
Otherwise, you would not have invented an air-conditioned movie theater in your room, Iggy."

77
00:04:30.953 --> 00:04:34.154
"Yeah," agreed Josh.

78
00:04:34.174 --> 00:04:38.896
"And it's a good thing you thought of showing The Magic Music Box.

79
00:04:40.176 --> 00:04:42.657
Otherwise, Tufty might have been lost forever!"

80
00:04:44.897 --> 00:04:47.818
"Luckily, Tufty could sing his telephone number!"

81
00:04:48.238 --> 00:04:48.958
added Jenny.

82
00:04:50.239 --> 00:04:54.940
So, as usual, my incredible inventions had worked.

83
00:04:56.236 --> 00:04:59.182
They just hadn't worked the way I expected them to!
